    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Full suite is green \u2014 **55 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured address form so the API accepts either the structured fields or the flat `address`, while staying backward-compatible.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** (`OwnerFields` schema) \u2014 added optional `addressLine1` and `addressLine2` properties, documented `address` as an accepted-on-input, composed-on-output field, and removed `address` from the `required` list (so an owner supplying only structured fields passes bean validation). `city` and `telephone` remain required.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (entity) \u2014 added `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` columns with getters/setters. They're optional (no `@NotEmpty`); the composed `address` keeps its existing `@NotEmpty`.\n\n3. **Schema SQL** (h2, hsqldb, postgres, mysql) \u2014 added `address_line1` / `address_line2` columns. (h2 is the active test profile; `ddl-auto=update` would also add them, but the explicit columns keep the scripts consistent.)\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 normalizes each supplied form up front (reusing the existing `normalizeAddress`: upper-case, whitespace collapse, `ST\u2192STREET`, etc.), prefers structured `addressLine1` when non-blank and falls back to the flat `address`, rejects the request when neither form is present, and composes the stored/returned `address` as normalized `addressLine1` with a single space + normalized `addressLine2` appended only when present. The normalized structured lines are stored (and cleared when the flat form was used).\n\nThe household hash, postcode validation, and locality already key off `city`/`postcode` (separate top-level fields present in both forms), so they read the effective address correctly with no further change.\n\n**Verification:** the three updated/new tests (`Cp01` required-either-form, `Cp12` structured normalization, `Cp44` normalize + compose + flat backward-compat) pass, and the full suite is green.",
